n: 3.11.2.5
name: reverse-closure-pair
kind: observation
is: In the old body a reversible rule names two hand-written closures. For Rust's let-int rule one closure builds an RS-BMF-LET node from the captures name and value, and the other rebuilds five tokens from the node's two children, typing the literal tokens a second time. bmf-roundtrip runs forward, backward, forward and compares the two nodes.
