n: 3.11.2.7
name: halves-never-joined
kind: finding
is: The old body holds the two halves of a reversible grammar in two engines and never joined them. The object engine applies a rule in both directions, with each direction written as a closure over tokens. The cursor engine holds pattern and template as data over text and applies a rule in one direction only.
status: inferred
conf: high
