name: one-node-test-before-cut
kind: observation
is: Before the cut, lang-convergence-band.fk asserted that each of two methods parsed from Go, Java and BML text equals its own hand-built node, and that the two nodes differ (three cells of 100, expected total 300). Go and Java each supplied three rules (method, param, ifs) over 13 shared rules; BML used its own 78-rule grammar, and by its rule text the BML third is not shown to reach the hand-built node. Types were read and not captured, so func f(x int) and func f(x string) gave the same node.
