n: 3.11.4
name: lens
kind: hub
is: The smallest mechanism the study found for one definition that reads, prints and translates. A lens is a list of rows (rule NAME PATTERN TEMPLATE) plus lexicon rows, all data; one interpreter matches the pattern to read and runs the template as a destructor to print. A 360-line C probe did so for Go, Java and Python texts of one method. A 2010 paper builds the same construction. Type-dependent operators, scope and text fidelity lie outside the rows.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-host-language-grammars

n: 3.11.4.1
name: nums-op-templates
kind: observation
is: In NUMS.Go, labels.yaml (298 lines) carries 81 _Op templates on neutral labels, for example Equal '{0} == {1}' and Ternary '{0} ? {1} : {2}': a literal sequence with numbered holes bound to the children of one label. The Go table Go.yaml (282 lines) carries none. Both files were last committed on 2023-04-05.
status: observed
src: 2.19.24#79 2.19.24#151 2.19.24#200 2.19.25 2.19.30#4 2.19.31#8 2.19.1#7
