n: 3.11.4.8
name: invertible-syntax-paper
kind: observation
is: The 2010 paper Invertible Syntax Descriptions builds one description that is parser and printer from partial isomorphisms: a constructor one way, a destructor the other; the printer takes alternatives in order, the parser keeps all of them. A priority filter prints parentheses only where the parser needs them. Stated limits: round trip up to equivalence classes; exponential worst case.
status: relayed
src: 2.19.26#3.1 2.19.26#4.4 2.19.26#6.4 2.19.1#8.3
limit: The study read pages 1 to 12 of the PDF, and review 9.5.16.24 read all 12 pages again.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-host-language-grammars

n: 3.11.4.9
name: bnfc-and-sdf3
kind: observation
is: BNFC generates abstract syntax, lexer, parser and printer from one labelled grammar for six target languages; its printer drops redundant separators, comments do not reach the parser, and layout syntax exists only in the Haskell-family back ends. A Spoofax SDF3 template production carries its layout; without templates the printer writes one line.
status: relayed
src: 2.19.27 2.19.28 2.19.29 2.19.1#8.3
limit: Read through a summarising fetch on 2026-11-24.
