n: 3.11.4.10
name: types-and-names-outside-rows
kind: finding
is: Two things a lens row cannot decide are not syntax. Operator meaning by operand type: Go's / is integer or real division, and the probe's Go lens is wrong for float64 operands. Names: the probe keeps names as string leaves, so f(x) and f(y) are different nodes and a rename changes identity; a side table needs a reader that resolves scope.
status: inferred
conf: high
src: 2.19.17#13-14
from: 3.11.4.4 3.11.4.6 3.11.1.5
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-host-language-grammars

n: 3.11.4.11
name: round-trip-on-nodes-not-text
kind: finding
is: A lens round trip holds on nodes: reading a printed node gives that node. Printing a read text gives a canonical spelling: one space between tokens, the lens's layout, no redundant parentheses, no comments. Python layout is a pre-pass outside the rows, a name equal to a target keyword re-reads wrongly, and ordered choice needs hand-ordered rules.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.11.4.5 3.11.4.7 3.11.2.2
limit: Spacing and parentheses were seen in the probe; the loss of comments and the keyword collision are reasoned, not run.
at: 2026-11-24
by: r2/gap-host-language-grammars

